        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.185,
            0.069,
            0.488,
            0.086
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part I"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.37,
            0.11,
            0.629,
            0.132
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Chapter Summary"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.152,
            0.883,
            0.207
          ],
          "content": "π is the constant circumference to diameter ratio for all circles, and is approximately equal to $\\frac { 2 2 } { 7 }$ or 3.14."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.212,
            0.884,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": "The circumference of a circle is given by $\\mathsf { C } = 2 \\pi r _ { \\mathrm { i } }$ , where r is the radius of the circle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.256,
            0.883,
            0.301
          ],
          "content": "• The arc length of a circle is given by $l = 2 \\pi r \\times \\frac { \\Theta ^ { \\circ } } { 3 6 0 ^ { \\circ } }$ , where θ is the central angle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.306,
            0.802,
            0.336
          ],
          "content": "• The area of a triangle is given by $\\mathrm { A } = { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } }$ base times height."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.341,
            0.883,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": "• Heron’s formula for the area of a triangle in terms of its sides a, b, c:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.232,
            0.367,
            0.798,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": "$\\mathrm{area} = \\sqrt{s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c)}$ . where $s = s = \\frac{1}{2}(a + b + c).$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.406,
            0.599,
            0.427
          ],
          "content": "• The area of a circle is given by $A = \\pi r^{2}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.435,
            0.884,
            0.538
          ],
          "content": "Estimates for π: Archimedes: $3 \\frac { 1 0 } { 7 1 } < \\pi < 3 \\frac { 1 } { 7 } ;$ Chongzhi: $\\pi \\; \\approx \\; \\frac { 3 5 5 } { 1 1 3 } ;$ Āryabhaṭa: $\\pi \\; \\approx \\; 3.1416;$ Mādhava’s exact formula: $\\pi = 4 \\left( 1 - \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{5} - \\frac{1}{7} + \\cdots \\right)$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.539,
            0.467,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": "• π is an irrational number."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.559,
            0.883,
            0.609
          ],
          "content": "• The area of a sector of a circle is given by $\\mathrm{area} = \\pi r^2 \\times \\frac{\\theta^\\circ}{360^\\circ}$ where θ is the central angle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.616,
            0.884,
            0.655
          ],
          "content": "Brahmagupta’s formula for the area of a cyclic quadrilateral in terms of its sides $a,b,c,d;$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.194,
            0.657,
            0.833,
            0.694
          ],
          "content": "$\\mathrm{area} = \\sqrt{(s - a)(s - b)(s - c)(s - d)}$ . where $\\frac{1}{2}(a + b + c + d)$"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
